https://github.com/tmeff5658-dotcom/stark-all-faces/tree/main/*
  oled_faces_v3.ino - STARK robot faces, 22 faces (SSD1306 128x64, I2C, ESP32)

  Wiring : SDA = GPIO21, SCL = GPIO22, VCC = 3.3V, GND, address 0x3C
  Libs   : Adafruit GFX Library + Adafruit SSD1306

  DEMO   : shows the boot splash, then every face for 5 s with a dissolve between faces.
           Serial Monitor (115200): send 'n' = next face, 'p' = previous face.

  FACES (same order as the enum)
    IDLE         neutral, does a small action every 10-20 s: looks around, winks or yawns
    HAPPY, SAD, THINKING, ANGRY
    LISTENING    wide eyes + sound bars (mic is recording)
    LOADING_BAR  eyes scan + scanner bar     (waiting for the AI server)
    LOADING_REACTOR  spinning arc reactor    (same meaning, Stark style)
    SPEAKING     mouth moves like speech
    DIZZY        spiral eyes (during the "spin" command)
    SLEEPING     closed eyes and floating z; wakeUp() opens the eyes slowly
    CONFUSED     "?" above one eye (the sentence was not understood)
    SURPRISED    wide eyes with small pupils and an "o" mouth
    TURN_LEFT / TURN_RIGHT   eyes look to that side + moving arrows (turn signal)
    STUCK        X eyes + "I am stuck"
    NO_WIFI      crossed WiFi icon (the robot works with its stored phrases)
    LOW_BATTERY  tired eyes + blinking battery icon
    RADAR        the 3 distance readings of the sensor servo (30, 90, 150 degrees)
    TRANSCRIPT   what the robot heard and what it will say
    HEART        beating heart eyes (for "good robot")
    WINK         wink with a smile

  HOW THE ROBOT LOGIC USES THIS FILE LATER (AUTO_CYCLE = false)
    setFace(FACE_LISTENING, millis());      // mic recording
    setFace(FACE_LOADING_BAR, millis());    // audio sent, waiting for the PC
    setFace(FACE_SPEAKING, millis());       // reply audio playing
    setMicLevel(0.0 .. 1.0);                // real mic loudness  -> LISTENING bars
    setSpeakLevel(0.0 .. 1.0);              // real speaker loudness -> SPEAKING mouth
    setBattery(percent);                    // -> LOW_BATTERY icon
    setRadar(cmAt30, cmAt90, cmAt150);      // -> RADAR   (0 or less = no echo)
    setTranscript("turn left", "Turning left");
    wakeUp(millis());                       // from SLEEPING: PIR motion or the robot's name

  WHEN IS THE ROBOT "STUCK"?  (decided by the movement code, not here)
    - the 3 scan readings (30, 90, 150 degrees) are ALL closer than STUCK_CM (about 20 cm), or
    - 3 avoidance turns in a row within 10 s and the front is still blocked.
    Then: setFace(FACE_STUCK, ...), say "I am stuck", stop the motors, wait for a voice command.
*/

